# Migrations

This directory contains Alembic database migrations for the Firebuster app.

Each migration file in `versions/` represents a single schema change (e.g. creating a table, adding a column). Migrations are versioned and chained — each one knows which revision it builds on, so Alembic can apply or revert them in order.

## Up and down migrations

Every migration has two functions:

- `upgrade()` — applies the change. Run when deploying new code.
- `downgrade()` — reverses the change. Run when rolling back.

Always implement both. A migration without a working `downgrade()` cannot be safely rolled back in production.

## Creating a migration

When you change a model, create a new migration file:

```bash
docker compose exec app uv run alembic revision -m "describe_your_change"
```

Fill in `upgrade()` and `downgrade()` in the generated file under `versions/`.

## Applying migrations

The stack must be running. Use the Makefile commands from the project root:

```bash
make migrate          # apply all pending migrations
make migrate-down     # roll back the last migration
make migrate-status   # show current migration state
```

## Keeping migrations healthy

- Never edit or delete an existing migration that has been applied in production — create a new one instead.
- Each migration should do one focused thing.
- Test both `upgrade` and `downgrade` locally before merging.
